{
  "caption": "**a**, Volcano plot (Treated vs control). Each point is one feature; 3,824 features with an adjusted P value are shown (176 features with adjusted P = NA after independent filtering are not shown). Red, up-regulated (n = 184); blue, down-regulated (n = 178); grey, not significant (n = 3,462). Significance: adjusted P < 0.05 and |log2 fold change| > 1 (DESeq2 Wald test, apeglm shrinkage, Benjamini-Hochberg). Dashed lines mark these thresholds. The 10 most significant features per direction are labelled. **b**, Principal component analysis of 8 samples using the 500 most variable features (centred, not scaled; axes NOT on a common scale because the two components span very different ranges). Each point is one sample, coloured by condition and shaped by batch. Percentages give the variance explained by each component. **c**, Expression of the 20 features with the smallest adjusted P values. Values are row z-scores of transformed expression, clipped at ±2; rows are ordered by hierarchical clustering (Euclidean distance, complete linkage) and columns by condition. 0 cells were clipped.",
